.\" WORKFLINT_UPDATE_MAN=1 cargo nextest run -p workflint man:: to update it.
.TH WORKFLINT 1 "" "workflint" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
workflint \- linter for GitHub Actions workflow files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B workflint
[check] [FLAGS] [FILES...] [\-]
.br
.B workflint
completion bash|zsh|fish|powershell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
workflint is a linter for GitHub Actions workflow files, compatible with
actionlint.
.PP
To check all YAML files in the current repository, run workflint without
arguments. It finds the nearest '.github/workflows' directory:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ workflint
.fi
.RE
.PP
To check specific files, pass their paths as arguments:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ workflint file1.yaml file2.yaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
A directory checks the YAML files under it, and workflint expands a quoted
glob itself:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ workflint .github 'docs/**/*.yaml'
.fi
.RE
.PP
To check text that is not saved in a file, such as the output of another
command, pass \- as the only argument. workflint reads it from stdin:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ workflint \-
.fi
.RE
.PP
To print errors as JSON, pass json or jsonl to the \-format flag. The
flag also takes a Go template, as in actionlint:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ workflint \-format json
$ workflint \-format '{{json .}}'
.fi
.RE
.PP
In GitHub Actions, \-format github prints annotations, and \-output writes
more formats to files in the same run:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ workflint \-format github \-output sarif=workflint.sarif
.fi
.RE
.PP
To complete flags in bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell, load the script that
workflint completion prints for the shell:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ eval "$(workflint completion bash)"
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-color
Always enable colorful output, even when NO_COLOR is set or stdout is not a terminal
.TP
.BI \-config " string"
Same as \-config\-file
.TP
.BI \-config\-file " string"
File path to config file. It replaces the config file of each project
.TP
.B \-debug
Enable debug output (for development). It includes the verbose output
.TP
.BI \-format " string"
Custom template to format error messages in Go template syntax, or the name of a format: github, json, jsonl, sarif, or summary. The command\-line documentation lists the template's fields and functions
.TP
.B \-help
Print the usage to stderr and exit. \-h is the same flag
.TP
.BI \-ignore " value"
Regular expression in Go syntax. Errors whose message it matches are not reported. This flag is repeatable
.TP
.B \-init\-config
Generate default config file at .github/workflint.yaml in current project
.TP
.BI \-jobs " int"
Maximum number of external tool processes, such as shellcheck, that run at once. The default is the number of CPUs
.TP
.B \-no\-color
Disable colorful output
.TP
.B \-oneline
Use one line per one error. Useful for reading error messages from programs
.TP
.BI \-output " value"
Also write the errors to a file, as FORMAT=PATH, such as sarif=results.sarif. FORMAT is github, json, jsonl, sarif, or summary. The summary format appends to the file. This flag is repeatable
.TP
.BI \-pyflakes " string"
Command name or file path of "pyflakes" external command. If empty, pyflakes integration will be disabled. If given, pyflakes checks Python scripts whatever python.linter says (default "pyflakes")
.TP
.B \-q
Same as \-quiet
.TP
.B \-quiet
Print only errors and fatal messages: no summary and no logs
.TP
.BI \-shellcheck " string"
Command name or file path of "shellcheck" external command. If empty, shellcheck integration will be disabled (default "shellcheck")
.TP
.B \-shellcheck\-cache
Keep the findings of shellcheck in a cache on disk, so that a later run does not check the same script again. The config key shellcheck.cache does the same for one project
.TP
.B \-silent
Print only fatal messages. The exit code tells whether errors were found
.TP
.BI \-stdin\-filename " string"
File name when reading input from stdin (default "<stdin>")
.TP
.B \-summary
Print the number of errors by severity to stderr
.TP
.B \-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.B \-version
Show version and how this binary was installed
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No errors, also when \-ignore or the config dropped every error. \-h, \-help, \-version, completion, and a successful \-init\-config exit with 0 too.
.TP
.B 1
At least one error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is invalid.
.TP
.B 3
A fatal error, such as a file or a config file that cannot be read, no workflow file to lint, an invalid \-ignore pattern or \-format template, or a shellcheck that \-shellcheck names and that is not found.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When not empty, turns color off unless \-color is given.
.TP
.B TERM
dumb turns color off unless \-color is given.
.TP
.B WORKFLINT_INSTALLED_FROM
The second line of \-version.
.TP
.B RAYON_NUM_THREADS
The number of files linted at once. The output is the same for every value.
.TP
.B PATH
Where \-shellcheck looks up a bare name.
.TP
.B SHELLCHECK_OPTS
Options that shellcheck reads. workflint passes its environment on to shellcheck.
